                <pb facs="1325" n="1313" xml:id="pg1313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90J/1–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at Aden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-27T21:00:00-04:00">January 27, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Your proposed informal visit to the Yemen meets with Department’s approval.
                    Bearing in mind that this Government has not accorded official recognition to
                    the Yemen, you should listen to such proposals or suggestions as Yemeni
                    officials may make to you, stating that you will be glad to convey them to your
                    Government, but you should, of course, make no commitments of any kind.</p>
                <p>Please report fully to Department upon your visit.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
